<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  folio-assistant — getting started: from "create a folio" to a live site.

  Source of truth: this file. Open it in bpmn.io, Camunda Modeler, or any other
  BPMN 2.0 tool. The SVG under docs/assets/img/workflows/ is generated from it
  by `bun run render:bpmn` — never hand-edit the SVG.

  The shape of this process is an argument about one sentence. "Create a folio"
  is asked by at least five different people wanting five different things:

    new-repo      never used folio-assistant, wants a folio in a fresh repo
    overlay       has a repository already, wants folio-assistant laid over it
    add-folio     is already in an instance, wants a second folio at top level
    new-content   is already in a folio, and meant a DOCUMENT, not a folio
    ask           the filesystem cannot tell, so the agent must

  Gateway_Intent does NOT let the agent pick. It carries <folio:decision/>, so
  the branch is computed by decisions/folio-intent.dmn from three facts, one of
  which is what the user actually said. `ask` is one of the outcomes the table
  can return — which is what makes asking obligatory rather than polite.

  Gateway_Live is the same construction applied to publication: `live`,
  `not-yet` and `unknown` are three states, and the third is never dressed up as
  either of the others.

  Enforcement is strict. Three steps are non-relaxable and each for the same
  kind of reason — they are the points where the process is acting on somebody
  else's repository or on their behalf:

    Task_ReadFacts       scaffolding without looking first is how a folio gets
                         written over somebody's project
    Gateway_Intent       the triage itself; relaxing it restores the bug
    Task_ConfirmImport   nobody's files are moved or imported on inference

  The <folio:skill> extension on an activity names the folio-assistant skill
  that implements it; <folio:bean> marks a step that reads or writes the shared
  work plan in beans/.
-->
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL"
                  xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC"
                  xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:folio="https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/bpmn"
                  id="Definitions_GettingStarted"
                  targetNamespace="https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/workflows"
                  exporter="folio-assistant" exporterVersion="1">
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collaboration_GettingStarted">
    <bpmn:participant id="Participant_GettingStarted" name="Getting started — &quot;create a folio&quot; to a live site" processRef="Process_GettingStarted" />
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_GettingStarted" name="Getting started" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>folio-assistant — getting started: from "create a folio" to a live site.

      "Create a folio" is five different requests. Gateway_Intent computes which one
      from decisions/folio-intent.dmn rather than letting the agent assume, and `ask`
      is one of the outcomes the table can return. Gateway_Live applies the same
      construction to publication, with `unknown` kept distinct from `not-yet`.

      Source of truth: this file. The SVG under docs/assets/img/workflows/ is
      generated from it by `bun run render:bpmn` — never hand-edit the SVG.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:extensionElements>
      <folio:policy enforcement="strict" />
    </bpmn:extensionElements>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="Process_GettingStarted_LaneSet">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_User" name="User (person)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Answers the one question Gateway_Intent cannot compute for itself — "ask" is one of five outcomes decisions/folio-intent.dmn can return — and, only on the overlay path, three further questions a repo scan cannot answer on its own: what to import, where it goes, and who does the importing.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:extensionElements><folio:role ref="user"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>StartEvent_AskToStart</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_AskIntent</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_ConfirmImport</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Agent" name="Onboarding agent (system)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Every write in this diagram belongs to this lane, and each sits behind the non-relaxable read-first gate: nothing is created or scaffolded until Gateway_Intent has classified what was actually asked for, which is what stands between this lane and writing over somebody's existing project.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:extensionElements><folio:role ref="onboarding-agent"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_DetectModality</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_ReadFacts</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gateway_Intent</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_ScanRepo</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_CreateRepo</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>EndEvent_HandOff</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Scaffold</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_WorkPlan" name="Work plan (beans)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Seeds one bean per top-level content object the author named, positioned after scaffolding but before the Pages probe — a work plan exists for a folio whose publication status is not yet known, rather than waiting on that answer.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:extensionElements><folio:role ref="work-plan"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_SeedPlan</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Publish" name="Publish — GitHub Pages">
        <bpmn:documentation>Derives the URL and holds the three-way report that follows it: "live", "not-yet" and "unknown" are reached by exclusive branches of one DMN-computed gateway, and this lane is what keeps a failed probe from being reported as the softer "not-yet" it would be tempting to default to.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:extensionElements><folio:role ref="publish-target"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_PagesBootstrap</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gateway_Live</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_ReportUrl</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_ReportPending</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_ReportUnknown</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>EndEvent_Ready</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>

    <bpmn:startEvent id="StartEvent_AskToStart" name="&quot;create a folio&quot;">
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>

    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_DetectModality" name="Detect the interaction
modality">
      <bpmn:documentation>Before the first question is asked, establish HOW to ask it: audio, ordinary chat, selectable options for a user with limited hand function, large-type for low vision. A user who finds the questions unusable never reaches the rest of this diagram.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:skill ref="interaction-modality" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>

    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_ReadFacts" name="Read the repository
facts">
      <bpmn:documentation>Mechanical, read-only: does a `&lt;name&gt;.config.json` declare a contentType, does the working tree hold somebody's existing project, and what has the user actually said. These are the three inputs to folio-intent.dmn. Non-relaxable: scaffolding without looking first is how a folio gets written over somebody's project.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:policy relaxable="false" />
        <folio:skill ref="getting-started" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_answer</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>

    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gateway_Intent" name="What is the user
asking for?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Computed, not chosen. decisions/folio-intent.dmn returns one of five branches from statedIntent, isFolio and repoHasContent. Non-relaxable: this gateway IS the fix.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:policy relaxable="false" />
        <folio:decision ref="decisions/folio-intent.dmn#Decision_FolioIntent" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_ask</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_overlay</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_newrepo</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_newcontent</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_addfolio</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>

    <bpmn:userTask id="Task_AskIntent" name="Choose from the
offered options">
      <bpmn:documentation>The question is presented as a short list of selectable options, never as free prose, and the list names the top-level content types the agent knows about. The answer becomes the statedIntent fact and the table is evaluated again — the user's answer is read as evidence, like any other fact.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:skill ref="interaction-modality" />
        <folio:skill ref="getting-started" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_ask</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_answer</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>

    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_ScanRepo" name="Scan the repo for
content worth importing">
      <bpmn:documentation>Read-only. Classifies candidates into library/ (external source) and content/ (authored here), and reports what it could not classify as its own bucket rather than forcing every file into one of the two.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:skill ref="repo-conversion" />
        <folio:skill ref="document-intake" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_overlay</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_scan</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>

    <bpmn:userTask id="Task_ConfirmImport" name="Import what, where,
and who does it">
      <bpmn:documentation>Three questions the scan cannot answer: import these or not; library or content for each group; leave the files where they are or reorganize to declutter. Plus whether to dispatch one ingestion agent or a small swarm. Non-relaxable: nobody's files are moved or imported on inference.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:policy relaxable="false" />
        <folio:skill ref="repo-conversion" />
        <folio:skill ref="dispatch-agent" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_scan</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_confirm</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>

    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_CreateRepo" name="Create the
repository">
      <bpmn:documentation>Only on the new-repo branch, and only after the user has named it. An empty working directory is scaffolded in place instead.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:skill ref="repo-conversion" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_newrepo</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_created</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>

    <bpmn:endEvent id="EndEvent_HandOff" name="Handed to content
authoring">
      <bpmn:documentation>The misspeak case. The user has a folio and wants a document in it; this process ends and authoring-a-document.bpmn or authoring-a-paper.bpmn begins. Ending here rather than scaffolding is the whole value of the triage.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_newcontent</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>

    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_Scaffold" name="Scaffold the folio
(folio_init)">
      <bpmn:documentation>content/, uploads/, library/, the first manifests, &lt;slug&gt;.json and &lt;slug&gt;.config.json, the builder shim, AGENTS.md with its stubs, .mcp.json, the session-start hook and the beans store. Refuses rather than overwrites when a folio is already present.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:skill ref="getting-started" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_addfolio</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_confirm</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_created</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_seed</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>

    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_SeedPlan" name="Seed the work plan">
      <bpmn:documentation>The first beans: what the author said they want to get started on, one bean per top-level content object they named.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:skill ref="todo-manager" />
        <folio:bean op="claim" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_seed</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_pages</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>

    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_PagesBootstrap" name="Start the Pages build
and derive the URL">
      <bpmn:documentation>scripts/pages-bootstrap.ts: derive the site URL from the git remote or &lt;name&gt;.config.json, report whether a publish workflow exists, and optionally probe until the site answers.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:skill ref="getting-started" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_pages</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_probe</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>

    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gateway_Live" name="Is the site
answering?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Computed from decisions/pages-live-gate.dmn. Three outcomes, and `unknown` is not a softer `not-yet`.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:decision ref="decisions/pages-live-gate.dmn#Decision_PagesLive" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_probe</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_live</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_notyet</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_unknown</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>

    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_ReportUrl" name="Hand over the
live link">
      <bpmn:documentation>Confirmed live. The link is given as a link, and the author is told what is on it.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:skill ref="getting-started" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_live</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_done1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>

    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_ReportPending" name="Say where it
will be">
      <bpmn:documentation>A measured 404. The author is told the address and that the first build has not landed there yet — which is useful, and is not the same as being told it is live.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:skill ref="getting-started" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_notyet</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_done2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>

    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_ReportUnknown" name="Say it could not
be confirmed">
      <bpmn:documentation>No URL, no probe, or a failed request. Reported as "could not check", never as "not yet" and never as "live".</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:skill ref="getting-started" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_unknown</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_done3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>

    <bpmn:endEvent id="EndEvent_Ready" name="Ready to author">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_done1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_done2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_done3</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>

    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_1" sourceRef="StartEvent_AskToStart" targetRef="Task_DetectModality" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_2" sourceRef="Task_DetectModality" targetRef="Task_ReadFacts" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_3" sourceRef="Task_ReadFacts" targetRef="Gateway_Intent" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_ask" name="ask" sourceRef="Gateway_Intent" targetRef="Task_AskIntent" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_answer" sourceRef="Task_AskIntent" targetRef="Task_ReadFacts" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_overlay" name="overlay" sourceRef="Gateway_Intent" targetRef="Task_ScanRepo" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_newrepo" name="new-repo" sourceRef="Gateway_Intent" targetRef="Task_CreateRepo" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_newcontent" name="new-content" sourceRef="Gateway_Intent" targetRef="EndEvent_HandOff" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_addfolio" name="add-folio" sourceRef="Gateway_Intent" targetRef="Task_Scaffold" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_scan" sourceRef="Task_ScanRepo" targetRef="Task_ConfirmImport" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_confirm" sourceRef="Task_ConfirmImport" targetRef="Task_Scaffold" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_created" sourceRef="Task_CreateRepo" targetRef="Task_Scaffold" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_seed" sourceRef="Task_Scaffold" targetRef="Task_SeedPlan" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_pages" sourceRef="Task_SeedPlan" targetRef="Task_PagesBootstrap" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_probe" sourceRef="Task_PagesBootstrap" targetRef="Gateway_Live" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_live" name="live" sourceRef="Gateway_Live" targetRef="Task_ReportUrl" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_notyet" name="not-yet" sourceRef="Gateway_Live" targetRef="Task_ReportPending" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_unknown" name="unknown" sourceRef="Gateway_Live" targetRef="Task_ReportUnknown" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_done1" sourceRef="Task_ReportUrl" targetRef="EndEvent_Ready" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_done2" sourceRef="Task_ReportPending" targetRef="EndEvent_Ready" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_done3" sourceRef="Task_ReportUnknown" targetRef="EndEvent_Ready" />
  </bpmn:process>

  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="Diagram_GettingStarted">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="Plane_GettingStarted" bpmnElement="Collaboration_GettingStarted">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Participant_GettingStarted_di" bpmnElement="Participant_GettingStarted" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="2280" height="960" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_User_di" bpmnElement="Lane_User" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="190" y="80" width="2250" height="150" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_Agent_di" bpmnElement="Lane_Agent" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="190" y="230" width="2250" height="360" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_WorkPlan_di" bpmnElement="Lane_WorkPlan" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="190" y="590" width="2250" height="110" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_Publish_di" bpmnElement="Lane_Publish" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="190" y="700" width="2250" height="340" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>

      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="StartEvent_AskToStart_di" bpmnElement="StartEvent_AskToStart"><dc:Bounds x="240" y="137" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_AskIntent_di" bpmnElement="Task_AskIntent"><dc:Bounds x="790" y="115" width="150" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_ConfirmImport_di" bpmnElement="Task_ConfirmImport"><dc:Bounds x="1080" y="115" width="150" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_DetectModality_di" bpmnElement="Task_DetectModality"><dc:Bounds x="330" y="260" width="150" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_ReadFacts_di" bpmnElement="Task_ReadFacts"><dc:Bounds x="520" y="260" width="150" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Gateway_Intent_di" bpmnElement="Gateway_Intent"><dc:Bounds x="730" y="275" width="50" height="50" /><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="600" y="345" width="140" height="27" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_ScanRepo_di" bpmnElement="Task_ScanRepo"><dc:Bounds x="880" y="350" width="150" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_CreateRepo_di" bpmnElement="Task_CreateRepo"><dc:Bounds x="880" y="440" width="150" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="EndEvent_HandOff_di" bpmnElement="EndEvent_HandOff"><dc:Bounds x="900" y="537" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_Scaffold_di" bpmnElement="Task_Scaffold"><dc:Bounds x="1320" y="260" width="150" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_SeedPlan_di" bpmnElement="Task_SeedPlan"><dc:Bounds x="1560" y="605" width="150" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_PagesBootstrap_di" bpmnElement="Task_PagesBootstrap"><dc:Bounds x="1560" y="720" width="150" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Gateway_Live_di" bpmnElement="Gateway_Live"><dc:Bounds x="1790" y="735" width="50" height="50" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_ReportUrl_di" bpmnElement="Task_ReportUrl"><dc:Bounds x="1900" y="720" width="150" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_ReportPending_di" bpmnElement="Task_ReportPending"><dc:Bounds x="1900" y="830" width="150" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_ReportUnknown_di" bpmnElement="Task_ReportUnknown"><dc:Bounds x="1900" y="940" width="150" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="EndEvent_Ready_di" bpmnElement="EndEvent_Ready"><dc:Bounds x="2180" y="742" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>

      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_1_di" bpmnElement="Flow_1"><di:waypoint x="276" y="155" /><di:waypoint x="405" y="155" /><di:waypoint x="405" y="260" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_2_di" bpmnElement="Flow_2"><di:waypoint x="480" y="300" /><di:waypoint x="520" y="300" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_3_di" bpmnElement="Flow_3"><di:waypoint x="670" y="300" /><di:waypoint x="730" y="300" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_ask_di" bpmnElement="Flow_ask"><di:waypoint x="755" y="275" /><di:waypoint x="755" y="155" /><di:waypoint x="790" y="155" /><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="765" y="212" width="30" height="14" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
